      "content": "Simulating a full switch to 50 independent local modules in the first 48 hours introduces a high probability of initial disruption. We would likely see an increased likelihood of minor material shortages as the new localized integrations undergo real-time validation. The risk centers on immediate hand-off failures between the new autonomous modules rather than catastrophic system-wide collapse. I will run a detailed Monte Carlo simulation to quantify the expected critical shortage frequency for your presentation.",
